### Description
The Add-Waiting-Room request allows the user to add a waiting rooms for a subdomain of the organisation.

<br>

### Requirements
Values of the request: none
Objects: ''WaitingRoomVO''

<br>

### Request
To add a waiting rooms, no additional information needs to be added to the path of the request. 

All waiting rooms are added without reference to the subdomain for which the waiting room is defined.

For a detailed specification of which information is required to add a waiting room, an object``WaitingRoomVO`` with the following attributes needs to be defined in the body:
| Attribute   | &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; | Description  | &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; | Values | &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; | Name in Myra App |
|--------|--------|--------|--------|--------|--------|--------|
| ``name`` |   | The name of the waiting room. |   |``string``|   |Name|
|``maxConcurrent``|   |The maximum number of visitors allowed on the Origin server at the same time. As soon as the value is exceeded, each additional visitor is directed to the waiting room. |   |``integer``|   |Max Visitors|
|``sessionTimeout``|   |The duration in seconds for which an inactive session can access the Origin server. If the session is not accessed again during the time, access for the session is deactivated. |   |``integer``|   |Session Timeout (Min)|
|``waitRefresh``|   |The duration in seconds after which the waiting page is reloaded. If the session is not accessed again after the third reload, the session is removed from the queue. |   |``integer``|   |Waiting Page refresh (sec)|
|``vhostId``|   |The ID of the subdomains for which the waiting room is available. |   |``integer``|   ||
|``content``|   |The HTML-Code for the waiting room template. |   |``string``|   |Content|

<br>

The following attributes are optional:
| Attribute   | &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; | Description  | &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; | Values | &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; | Name in Myra App |
|--------|--------|--------|--------|--------|--------|--------|
|``paths``|   |a path within the apex domain or subdomain for which the waiting room is to be valid. The path need to be defined as a regular expression. The default value in the PATH field is ".". If the default value "." is used as the path, the waiting pages and settings of all waiting rooms with a path of the corresponding apex domain or subdomain are overwritten. |   |``string``|   |Path|
|``subDomainName``|   |The name of the subdomain for which the waiting room is available. |   |``string``|   |Subdomain|

<br>

The system responds by returning the object ``WaitingRoomVO`` with the information about the new entry.

<br>

>> ---
>> **Note:**
>> If the optional attributes are not set, the system adds a default value.
>> ---
>> **Note:**
>> The body does not include the attributes ``id``, ``created`` and ``modified``. The values for these attributes will be set by the system after the creation of the entry.
>> ---

**Waiting room content**
A waiting page is stored for each waiting room that is added using the Waiting Room function. Initially, there is a default template to choose from. You can also upload your own waiting page as an *.htm or *.html file.  placeholders are used to ensure that the waiting page displays all the necessary information about the waiting room correctly. A table with the most important placeholders can be found below:
| Variable name  | &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; | Description  | 
|----------------|----------------|----------------|
| ``!WAIT_REFRESH!`` |   |Defines the number of seconds between page refreshes. This variable needs to be included as a http-equiv=refresh meta tag inside of the HTML head in order for the page to reload automatically and give users feedback about their current position in the queue. |
|``!CURRENT_POSITION!`` |   |Shows the visitor’s position in the queue. |
|``!SUBDOMAIN!`` |   |Shows the host name without the protocol and path. |
|``!QUEUE_SIZE!`` |   |Shows the total number of visitors in the queue. |
|``!QUEUE_PROGRESS!`` |   |Displays the number of visitors after the user. Can be used to give visual feedback about queue progress, for example by defining a progress bar. |

<br>

**Example Template:**
```
<html lang="en">
    <head>
        <meta charset="UTF-8" />
        <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0" />
        <meta http-equiv="refresh" content="!WAIT_REFRESH!" />
        <title>!SUBDOMAIN! Waiting Room</title>
        <style>
            body {
                font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;
                font-optical-sizing: auto;
                font-style: normal;
                min-height: 100vh;
                margin: 0;
            }
            .background {
                background: linear-gradient(
                    133.66deg,
                    #7dff54 -13.21%,
                    #54ddc2 38.6%,
                    #003bcc 97.97%
                );
                display: flex;
                justify-content: center;
                align-items: center;
            }
            .card {
                background-color: #ffffff;
                width: clamp(400px, 60%, 800px);
            }
            .card-content {
                padding: min(4vw, 40px);
            }
            .progress-bar {
                -webkit-appearance: none;
                -moz-appearance: none;
                appearance: none;
                border: none;
                display: flex;
                color: #003bcc;
                width: 100%;
                height: 8px;
            }
```

